# Responsible autonomy

Scope: the entire Synthetic Society Lab monorepo. Recorded November 5, 2026.
The owner delegates decisions provided they are justified, logical, responsible
and bounded by caps and safeguards. This removes routine permission interruptions;
it supplies no new monetary amount and does not change past execution evidence.

- Proceed with ordinary implementation, tests, local commits, analysis and bounded recovery within the approved research scope. Explain material choices and record their purpose, evidence, limits and outcome.
- Keep the existing combined $5 cumulative ceiling, current E02 pilot $1 subceiling and E01 paid inference $0. Include settled costs and all outstanding reservations/uncertain holds. Never reset the ledger or create a new owner to obtain fresh allowance.
- Before any new live batch, record its fixed model-request count, input/output token bounds, spend reservation, finite billing-lookup/retry count, deadline and cancellation behavior. Enforce these in tested code. Use fresh verified prices and the approved provider/model constraints.
- A delayed billing record can be investigated through a separately recorded, bounded read-only recovery batch without another human permission request. Never resend a model prompt merely because its response or bill is uncertain. Keep the full hold until verified reconciliation through the established accounting path.
- Do not replay a consumed launcher, edit past approval packets, or erase failure evidence. Preserve the stopped run; use a separately versioned continuation with explicit ancestry and independently reviewed implementation. Retain the study protocol and matched comparison conditions.
- Stop at the first exhausted budget, request or time limit, unresolved integrity/identity problem, or unaccounted model dispatch. Preserve diagnostics and continue independent offline work. Do not silently fallback, enlarge samples or claim completion from partial results.
- Retain independent technical review for experimental milestones and changes to accounting/recovery code. Use that review to resolve implementation issues; it is not a substitute for owner authority or a reason to ask the owner about routine choices.
- Ask the owner only for an increased spending ceiling, materially different research scope, unavailable access or credentials, external publication, or destructive actions beyond the authorized work. Do not ask again for authority already supplied.
- Keep secrets and private source data out of Git and reports. Maintain the existing restrictions on political targeting, outreach and unsupported scientific claims.

Example: diagnose a delayed generation-statistics record, prepare and test a
bounded recovery, then reconcile the original generation without a second model
request. Record actual costs and remaining holds; do not relabel the stopped
pilot successful or infer an effect from its incomplete comparisons.

This policy records standing human discretion. It does not itself execute calls,
alter financial state, override enforced runtime limits, or schedule background work.
